# Coach speech (Dutch): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "je" ("jij" / "jouw" only for a
# contrast) and "ik" / "mijn" for himself; Dutch never shows the player's gender.
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   with their article ("de opening", "het middenspel", "het eindspel"): said
#                       after "in" or as a subject ("In {text} speelde je ...", "{text} was ...").
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement right after "Remise" ("Remise door herhaling van zetten.").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase in lower case ("je stukken gedekt houden"), always said
#                       after a colon ("Iets om te oefenen: ...", "Een tip: ...").
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach page's level name in quotation marks, said after "niveau"
#                       ("op niveau “Clubspeler”").
# Forms used (common.lang): {moves:move} = "34 zetten"; {n:best_move} = "5 beste zetten";
# {acc:percent} = "85%" (spoken "vijfentachtig procent"), used for every accuracy figure;
# {opening:def} = the opening's name with its article, inside a sentence; {opening} alone after a colon.
# Move numbers are cardinals: "bij zet {n}", "zet {n}". Pieces captured include the pawns, and "stuk"
# does not: the count is said as how many times the player captured ("{n:time} geslagen").

